  "strategy": ".../strategy>\n\nThis detailed implementation plan outlines an optimized approach to minimize the step function sequence objective within strict time and resource constraints. It leverages gradient-based optimization with momentum and adaptive learning rate for numerical stability, combined with sophisticated line search strategies for efficient progress.\n\nThe core idea is to cast the optimization problem into a gradient-descent framework with momentum, enhancing robustness for large sequences and complex landscapes. The algorithm includes:\n\n1. Progressive line search initialization using signed-based convolution to quickly approach promising points\n2. Repeated objective evaluation to ensure strong candidate acceptance\n3. Shot-noise sampling for controlled exploration under resource limitations\n4. Ordered, structured optimization phases with explicit timing management\n5. Progressive boundary relaxation and structured restarts to escape local minima\n6. Phase tracking with log management to monitor time utilization\n\nThe detailed steps are:\n\n1. Rationale:\n   - The previous algorithm showed good convergence but could benefit from gradient-based methods optimized for the exact objective function\n   - We maintain the core constraint-handling while introducing strictly gradient-based optimization for better responsiveness\n   - We reduce hyperparameter complexity but expand dependencies from trusted math libraries\n\n2. Implementation:\n   - Initialization: Use `compute_conv` and `smoothed_gradient` for accurate gradient calculation\n   - Iterative Optimization: Progressive value systems with time-slot allocation\n   - Candidate Management: Maintain best candidate separately for comparison\n   - Term conditions: Responsive timing and gradient stability checks\n\nThe exact implementation follows technical standards with:\n\n- No implicit steps - only explicit calls to trusted libraries (numpy, scipy)\n- All core optimizations are numeric and gradient-dispatchable\n- No protocol extension outside standard behavior\n\nExecution track:\n- Phase1: (200 seconds) Coarse line search with momentum to establish baseline\n- Phase2: (200 seconds) Intensive gradient-based polishing for rapid convergence\n- Phase3: (500 seconds) Progressive learning rate and restart phases for escape strategies\n- Phase4: (600 seconds) Focused optimization with linearity checks and precision enhancements\n\nAll operations are fully justified and numerically handled without arbitrary abstraction.",
